# NAB - National Australia Bank

> NAB (National Australia Bank) is one of Australia's "Big Four" banks, serving over 8 million customers with personal, business, and corporate banking products and services. Founded in 1858, NAB is headquartered in Melbourne, Victoria and operates across Australia and internationally.

Important information:

- NAB provides banking products including transaction accounts, savings accounts, home loans, credit cards, personal loans, business lending, and insurance
- Any advice on the website is general in nature and does not consider individual objectives, financial situation or needs
- Credit applications are subject to credit assessment criteria. Interest rates, fees and charges are subject to change
- Target Market Determinations for products are available at nab.com.au/TMD
- National Australia Bank Limited ABN 12 004 044 937 AFSL and Australian Credit Licence 230686

